      "writtenOn": "2020-01-13T18:05:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Specify what the client should do when the user stops interacting.\n\nFor instance, if the client calls:\n\nsetUserInteractionBoost(60000); // 1 minute\n\nThen the user decides to close their phone, should setUserInteractionBoost(1) be called to time out quickly? Do we need stopUserInteractionBoost?\n\n\nAlso, document what times are expected here? Should it mean a few milliseconds, this will get called, with ever screen-touch, or are longer durations expected?",
